The legal texts come from the Registro Oficial of the Republic of Ecuador:

  Source: Registro Oficial del Ecuador, órgano de la Corte Constitucional,
  https://www.registroficial.gob.ec, retrieved 28 October 2026.

The Registro Oficial states no licence for its editions. They are official legal texts of the Republic of Ecuador,
which are public.

Changes made by Lexifina: each gazette edition was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws,
rulings and referendums that made each change. The wording of the law was not changed. Where a later version was
rebuilt from an amending act, the text comes from that act as the Registro Oficial printed it (its text layer;
no OCR). The Registro Oficial does not endorse
this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
